# Normalise line endings so the repository does not show phantom changes
# on a Windows checkout. Text is stored with LF; batch files need CRLF to
# be reliable when run by cmd.exe.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.exe binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.bin binary

# Instrument data, kept byte for byte. These came off Tektronix disks or
# were written for an instrument to read, and `text=auto` would store
# them LF and hand back a file whose bytes are not the ones that went in.
# The i-Pattern masks are zero-padded so git spots those on its own; the
# setups, our own text masks and the generator's state files are not, and
# git was rewriting all 38 of them.
*.MSK binary
*.SET binary
*.sta binary
*.wfm binary
*.isf binary
